"P2580764987" "I am sure that you have noticed the Workbenches all over this facility.  You will be using them to invent. <br><br>Using the Workbench is simple: select the Recipe you want to use and click 'Create' to make something.  If you don't have the ingredients or the finances, you will be prevented from creating anything because the interface will be 'greyed out.'<br><br>You acquire Recipes by defeating mobs or receiving them as rewards.  You can only use them once, unless you've received special Badges that allow you to 'memorize' them, but that only applies to Common Recipes.  If you aren't sure which is which, then look at your Inventory or the Workbench window.  It'll tell you.<br><br>Now, let's talk about the results of the Workbench.  Recipes can build Enhancements and even Costume Parts. <br><br>You might want to arrange your Inventory before you start because if you don't have room you won't be able to build anything.  The Recipe display will alert you, too.<br><br>If all goes well, the result of your hard work will be dropped into your Enhancement Inventory.  Costume Parts work slightly differently.  You create them and they are 'unlocked', but you still have to visit a Tailor to pick them up.  See Rita at Rita's Remnants here in Imperial City and she will help you.<br><br>Now, for your exercise, approved by Cole of course.  <color orange>Go to that Visualization Console and investigate the intricate workings of Workbenches.</color>  There's plenty of data to be had, so you'll want to peruse the entire manual.  Print out the worksheets, fill them out with your data and thoughts, and then bring them back to me when you're done.  When you've completed the exercise, you will be ready for the honor and privilege of creating something."
// SendOffString :
"P3301770676" "Remember, researching workbenches and their results is only <i>part</i> of the exercise.  To truly enrich your mind, you need to print out the workbooks and fill in the answers with your personal insights."

